{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1265932-a-glimpse-of-the-aberrant-future-re-spoilers-please","id":1265932,"title":"A glimpse of the Aberrant future, re: spoilers,please?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-11-09T14:47:45-08:00","id":1265932,"title":"A glimpse of the Aberrant future, re: spoilers,please?","content":"So, is there anything those of us who backed the Scion Kickstarter could potentially extrapolate from there and make a guess as to how Novas will work? <br /> <br /> Also, can anyone in the know just flat-out <b><i>tell us</i></b> how it's going to work? <br /> <br /> Obviously, Tiers are going to be used in place of Mega-Attributes, which is a welcome relief if the Tiers for Mental and Social Attributes are explained clearly enough. Epic Physicals are easy enough to figure out; high-Tier Mental and Social capabilities are going to need some consideration and explanations. But I expect that we can deduce quite a few of those from the Sage and Lover Callings, with a few of the others also being noteworthy. <br /> <br /> Obviously, we'll have a three-stage Background process to sort out skills and such, one of which will be devoted to the Eruption process. I wonder if that Eruption phase can be boosted up a Tier just as the basic concept of a Scion can? It would make sense, as it would make sense for Novas to be able to have Calling-like powers.<br /> <br /> I imagine that the powers a nova possesses will also function like an umbrella for Knacks and Boon-like abilities that can only be used with Quantum. This allows character customization with a bit more free-form power approach. I also imagine that quantum will function much like Legend in Scion does, with a maximum of so many Quantum tied to the Quantum level. This makes Quantum points a bit more valuable than they were during first edition, and not just record-keeping. This also makes resource strategy a bit more important. <br /> <br /> I think Taint this time around will be a more voluntary thing to use when your Nova needs some extra Quantum, much like Fatebinding is in Scion. That is something I find that I can live with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T15:08:20-08:00","id":1265941,"title":"","content":"I am wondering how Powers will work. My best guess is we'll get a bunch of Power-specific Knacks and Boons to better customize Powers with, but will we also be able to take &quot;quirks&quot; or something that will limit Powers and maybe get some sort of cost rebate, or something similar as compensation? <br /> <br /> How will Invulnerability work this time around? It seemed like a go-to Power picked up by everyone just because. I wonder if there will be some sort of economy at work to keep players more conservative in their choices. I certainly see that at work in Scion; if you want to be good at a Purview, it's best to concentrate on it so that you can put you available Boons in it. Spreading yourself around makes you a jack-of-all-trades, but a master of none. <br /> <br /> Speaking of economies, will it be feasible to do my Swiss-army Nova, who concentrated on Mega-Atts in first edition? I always wanted to do that, but there was a concern that they'd get smeared into paste by other Novas who bought high-damage and high-defense Powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T15:12:26-08:00","id":1265942,"title":"","content":"While both use the Storypath system, Scion and Aberrant have quite different assumptions beneath their powers and considerations. I don\u2019t think there\u2019s a lot about how Aberrant works that can be extrapolated from Scion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T15:30:49-08:00","id":1265949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1265932-a-glimpse-of-the-aberrant-future-re-spoilers-please?p=1265942#post1265942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While both use the Storypath system, Scion and Aberrant have quite different assumptions beneath their powers and considerations. I don\u2019t think there\u2019s a lot about how Aberrant works that can be extrapolated from Scion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I know, but nonetheless I have a good feeling about the similarity in Taint and Fatebinding in this edition. I'm just wasting time pointlessly speculating because I'm in this primarily for Aberrant. <br /> <br /> <i>But let it be known</i>, what I've seen regarding Talents and Psions is pretty damn snazzy this time around. I was especially pleasantly surprised by Psions, in that having a diverse group of them pooling their resources adds some cool benefits. I was hoping they were going to find a way to do that during first edition, and I'm glad they hardwired it into second. I'd actually happily play a Psion this time around. I would not have said that during the first edition. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T17:22:14-08:00","id":1266007,"title":"","content":"Oh. I thought maybe this could be a thread for some tiny but fun Aberrant spoiler to make us smile. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> Also I'm pretty sure a lot of novas would be erupting in this political and social climate we have right now. <br /> <br /> Also Steve the designer is awesome and I'm looking forward to his, and his team's, work!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T17:59:21-08:00","id":1266028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1265932-a-glimpse-of-the-aberrant-future-re-spoilers-please?p=1265949#post1265949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>But let it be known</i>, what I've seen regarding Talents and Psions is pretty damn snazzy this time around. I was especially pleasantly surprised by Psions, in that having a diverse group of them pooling their resources adds some cool benefits. I was hoping they were going to find a way to do that during first edition, and I'm glad they hardwired it into second. I'd actually happily play a Psion this time around. I would not have said that during the first edition. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m so glad to read that. \ud83d\ude42","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T18:00:15-08:00","id":1266030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1265932-a-glimpse-of-the-aberrant-future-re-spoilers-please?p=1266007#post1266007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh. I thought maybe this could be a thread for some tiny but fun Aberrant spoiler to make us smile. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> Also I'm pretty sure a lot of novas would be erupting in this political and social climate we have right now. <br /> <br /> Also Steve the designer is awesome and I'm looking forward to his, and his team's, work!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would love to give spoilers, but I\u2019m not authorized to do so yet, and the NDA ninjas have my address!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-10T10:49:36-08:00","id":1266232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1265932-a-glimpse-of-the-aberrant-future-re-spoilers-please?p=1266030#post1266030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I would love to give spoilers, but I\u2019m not authorized to do so yet, and the NDA ninjas have my address!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Do not piss off NDA ninjas, for they are subtle and quick to strike. <br /> <br /> Ah well, I'll happily keep pointlessly speculating about Aberrant until it's time for spoilers to roam free. It still holds a special place in my gaming heart. And I'm quite heartened by the underlying system this time around. <br /> <br /> do they still need any playtesting done? (He asked hopefully, knowing full well the answer was &quot;no, thank you.&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-10T12:39:53-08:00","id":1266245,"title":"","content":"My main hope is a way to customize and tweak Powers in this game. I admit that I got spoiled by making Wild Talents my default Aberrant system for awhile. In that game, they <i>expect</i> you to tweak the powers and not just pick it out of a cafeteria. But if the Knacks and Boons system of Purviews makes it to Aberrant, it'll make assembling a more distinct Power easier. In fact, it'd be easier to gradually upscale a Power that starts out limited but gains a greater breadth of uses over time, which I wonder if that's what they'll be going towards. <br /> <br /> And another thing, of course, is to make Taint a player-focused thing rather than an arbitrary GM thing. I get the idea behind it, but I remember being sensitive to the first edition violating the division between player/GM duties, and allowing someone else to make a potentially profound change to my character that might shift it away from what I was envisioning. Fatebinding in Scion seems a bit more player-friendly in that it allows <i>the player</i> to make a critical choice. It may not seem like a difference, but to me it makes <i>all</i> the difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T16:23:39-08:00","id":1267118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1265932-a-glimpse-of-the-aberrant-future-re-spoilers-please#post1265932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, can anyone in the know just flat-out <b><i>tell us</i></b> how it's going to work?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. The core and Aeon aren't even out to the public yet; we're certainly not going to preview Aberrant material when the first two(!) core books haven't been seen yet, not to mention the first supplements (Aeon Aexpansion and In Media Res).<br /> <br /> Aberrant will have to wait.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T19:20:20-08:00","id":1268454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1265932-a-glimpse-of-the-aberrant-future-re-spoilers-please?p=1267118#post1267118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. The core and Aeon aren't even out to the public yet; we're certainly not going to preview Aberrant material when the first two(!) core books haven't been seen yet, not to mention the first supplements (Aeon Aexpansion and In Media Res).<br /> <br /> Aberrant will have to wait.</div> </div> </div> </div>But, but, aren't we supposed to have every single possible supplement for the next five years arriving in our mailboxes right this very second? Isn't that how Kickstarter is supposed to work!?!<br /> <br /> Yeah, no. No it isn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T04:56:01-08:00","id":1268516,"title":"","content":"Aberrant will get released 2019, though. Yes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T07:12:52-08:00","id":1268543,"title":"","content":"As a gentle reminder, I know full well that they're not going to spoil anything for Aberrant yet, I just hate how that sounds and am trying to relieve my impatience by brainstorming how the game might possibly look. I know full-well it'll both look eerily like Aberrant 1st in some ways, but will not in the least resemble it in others. I know things have to happen in their own time before this game can exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T11:35:01-08:00","id":1268595,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m going to counter part of the above statement I hope with everything that they Do Not Use That Stupid Tier System for Aberrant. Mega Stats are important for a Superhero type game the tier system just will not work right. You have mega strength but are you but are you Hulk strong, Thor strong, or Spider-Man Strong in this setting this is important. Also Novas are supposed a Superman type Hero\u2019s Scions can\u2019t lift Tanks or Battleships some Novas are supposed to be able to strength is their main power. I would agree the the power Tier is alright for Scion but please don\u2019t think it\u2019ll work for Aberrant","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6379-tytalan","name":"tytalan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T11:57:12-08:00","id":1268600,"title":"","content":"On rpg.net Ian Watson wrote that the Aberrant kickstarter should start next year at the same time of the Aeon one, so February or March.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5811-starkiller","name":"Starkiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T01:44:25-08:00","id":1268761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Starkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1265932-a-glimpse-of-the-aberrant-future-re-spoilers-please?p=1268600#post1268600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On rpg.net Ian Watson wrote that the Aberrant kickstarter should start next year at the same time of the Aeon one, so February or March.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In the interest of tempering expectations, what I said was &quot;<i>I think the hope is to do a Kickstarter early next year,</i>&quot; which is a different sort of statement than &quot;it should start early next year.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T11:31:48-08:00","id":1268924,"title":"","content":"Either way can\u2019t wait to read the new Aberrant, I loved the first edition and I have high expectations for the new one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5811-starkiller","name":"Starkiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T17:14:30-08:00","id":1269398,"title":"","content":"My hopes:<br /> <br /> Aberrant 1e came out before the Marvel Cinematic Universe. These days, Iron Man isn't an obscure B-List hero known only to comic book fans; he's front and center in popular culture. So Aberrant 2e needs to make Superscience more of a thing: heroes like Iron Man and Ant-Man need to be doable without resorting to calling them Stealth Novas. <br /> <br /> Likewise, street vigilantes and superspies should get some more support, again without calling them Stealth Novas. <br /> <br /> The above can be achieved to a large extent by referencing the Talents section of the core book; so it shouldn't take much in the way of page count. Just emphasize that Talents are right there alongside the Novas making an impression on the world. <br /> <br /> Then there are the Psiads. Not only should they be a thing in Aberrant, they should also have their own niche. That means that some Quantum Powers from 1e shouldn't be Quantum Powers in 2e. I'd remove Telepathy and ESP at a minimum, and probably a few others. I'd reintroduce them in the Aberrant Sidekick book (name pending) in a section dealing with Psychomorphs and \u201cMentalist Novas\u201d (the Nova counterpart to Quantakinetics) \u2014 and the Psychomorphs seen there would be compatible with the Psiads that we'll be getting in \u00c6on \u00c6xpansion. <br /> <br /> For the Novas themselves: Scale replaces Mega-Attributes, in that you can apply Scale to Attributes. You can also apply it to Quantum Powers, and possibly other things. 1e's Enhancements get renamed (I suggest Augmentations), regrouped (some groups will correlate with Attributes; others won't), and presented in opposition to Aberrations. Body Modifications gets recast as an Augmentation instead of a Quantum Power. Quantum Powers will be more customizable. But with an effort made to keep this from turning into yet another mechanics-centered system like Champions. I'd like something between M&amp;M (Kenson's homage to DC Heroes) and Icons (Kenson's homage to Marvel Superheroes).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T22:15:46-08:00","id":1269446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1265932-a-glimpse-of-the-aberrant-future-re-spoilers-please?p=1269398#post1269398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My hopes:<br /> <br /> Aberrant 1e came out before the Marvel Cinematic Universe. These days, Iron Man isn't an obscure B-List hero known only to comic book fans; he's front and center in popular culture. So Aberrant 2e needs to make Superscience more of a thing: heroes like Iron Man and Ant-Man need to be doable without resorting to calling them Stealth Novas. </div> </div> </div> </div>I believe I\u2019ve said it here before, but I\u2019ll say again - you absolutely can be an Iron Man or Ant-Man in Aberrant 2e. Or Iron Spider, or Black Panther, or a nova using just about any* of the tech in MCU films. The Superscience rules were written with those kinds of movies in mind. <br /> <br /> A starting character could be an Iron Man Mk 3 equivalent (or Mk 2 if you introduce some high-altitude icing Flaws in your suit design). Mark 50 is certainly doable, but would probably take a nova with around 10 years of MCU films experience to develop their skills and abilities sufficiently. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s entirely viable to build nova characters who focus on technology and Superscience-enhancing abilities, and express their power entirely through that means.<br /> <br /> *I\u2019ve gone through and done a broad spread of designs in the process of checking the rules. I look forward to being able to share them once the Kickstarter is in motion and the relevant chapter is released. But if there\u2019s any specific MCU tech people would like build-previewed when the Kickstarter happens, let me know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T02:07:55-08:00","id":1269771,"title":"","content":"Dataweaver I think you are completely missing the point of Aberrant. This is the time of Novas not marvel class superheroes. Novas are not street type hero\u2019s they are not Powerman or Ironfist they are young Gods. We need mega attributes, the Scion system completely fails to meet the power levels that are presented in Aberrant. This is the game of Superman and Wonderwoman just giving successes and bonuses will not do who can life and throw a Tank, who can do a battleship believe it or not these things are a major part of the setting. As for psiads they to don\u2019t fit the setting two much quantum suppressing their powers. <br /> <br /> I beg the developers please Don\u2019t turn Aberrant in to a pail imitation of its former glory the whole concept of the setting is man attempting to retain his humanity when given god like powers not marvel superheroes jr","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6379-tytalan","name":"tytalan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T02:55:54-08:00","id":1269780,"title":"","content":"There is room for multiple opinions regarding what flavor of 'superheroes' you can get in Aberrant -- it was always intended to allow for more Marvel style as well as DC. I believe that it's been said that the new edition is explicitly intended to support a range of styles as well.<br /> <br /> That said, I feel the need to address this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tytalan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1265932-a-glimpse-of-the-aberrant-future-re-spoilers-please?p=1269771#post1269771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for psiads they to don\u2019t fit the setting two much quantum suppressing their powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>First edition had psiads active in the Aberrant timeline, and there were rules for them in the Aberrant Player's Guide (it's heavily implied that Sophia Rousseau was one). Quantum doesn't really suppress their powers, though noetic and quantum powers rarely mix. But even if they weren't already established as existing in that time period, allowing psiads as viable player characters shouldn't have any actual affect on novas or the game as a whole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T03:47:00-08:00","id":1269782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tytalan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1265932-a-glimpse-of-the-aberrant-future-re-spoilers-please?p=1269771#post1269771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the game of Superman and Wonderwoman just giving successes and bonuses will not do who can life and throw a Tank, who can do a battleship believe it or not these things are a major part of the setting. As for psiads they to don\u2019t fit the setting two much quantum suppressing their powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>With respect, tytalan, if you think a few successes is all that scale does, you\u2019ve missed the point of the system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T06:45:06-08:00","id":1269801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1265932-a-glimpse-of-the-aberrant-future-re-spoilers-please?p=1269446#post1269446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But if there\u2019s any specific MCU tech people would like build-previewed when the Kickstarter happens, let me know.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be fun to maybe showcase some &quot;Not Quite Marvel&quot; and &quot;Not Quite DC&quot; heroes during the kickstarter to show off the system! I like this idea.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/22659-kickstarter-james","name":"Kickstarter James","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar22659_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T09:30:04-08:00","id":1269848,"title":"","content":"A not quite tony stark/iron man would be nice, it would illustrate a nova tech super genius plus how a gadget powered armor works. Also a Batman type could show a more \u201cstealth\u201c nova.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5811-starkiller","name":"Starkiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T10:51:26-08:00","id":1269867,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'd rather see a Batman type as an example of Talents in the Nova age. There is still room for what 1e called \u201cstealth Novas\u201d; but to my thinking, a Stealth Nova is what Adventure called a Stalwart: no Quantum Powers, just Augmentations and maybe a level or two of Scale here and there. Batman's big thing is that he <i>isn't</i> a metahuman, but manages to hold his own in a world where the likes of Superman and Wonder Woman are running around \u2014 that's definitely Talent territory. <br /> <br /> IMHO, the same ought to be sayable of the likes of Iron Man, Steel, or Hardware: powersuits should be considered Inspired Super-Science, not Powered Super-Science. Essentially, they're early VARGs, and could even be considered Advanced Super-Science if not for the fact that they're close to a century ahead of their time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T16:43:10-08:00","id":1269929,"title":"","content":"I'd wonder if it would be possible to blend Talents and Nova abilities. There was a character from DC in the 90s called Hitman. Tommy Monaghan was a freelance hired killed who got super-powers after being attacked by a fat alien vampire who drank spinal fluid (Bloodlines). After surviving, he found he had acquired the ability to read minds as well as X-ray Vison. Of course he was also extremely talented when using firearms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T09:47:20-08:00","id":1270371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1265932-a-glimpse-of-the-aberrant-future-re-spoilers-please?p=1269929#post1269929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd wonder if it would be possible to blend Talents and Nova abilities. There was a character from DC in the 90s called Hitman. Tommy Monaghan was a freelance hired killed who got super-powers after being attacked by a fat alien vampire who drank spinal fluid (Bloodlines). After surviving, he found he had acquired the ability to read minds as well as X-ray Vison. Of course he was also extremely talented when using firearms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not likely Talents are a powered type of individual in Trinity it\u2019s not just skill it\u2019s using the multiverses to get the out come you want. Just like Psions and Novas it\u2019s a path to a higher state of being ang no two of those can mix. You could have a very skilled character who becomes a Nova but that is different","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6379-tytalan","name":"tytalan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T21:39:49-08:00","id":1270764,"title":"","content":"[deleted because already answered]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T21:53:15-08:00","id":1270766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1265932-a-glimpse-of-the-aberrant-future-re-spoilers-please?p=1269867#post1269867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'd rather see a Batman type as an example of Talents in the Nova age. There is still room for what 1e called \u201cstealth Novas\u201d; but to my thinking, a Stealth Nova is what Adventure called a Stalwart: no Quantum Powers, just Augmentations and maybe a level or two of Scale here and there. Batman's big thing is that he <i>isn't</i> a metahuman, but manages to hold his own in a world where the likes of Superman and Wonder Woman are running around \u2014 that's definitely Talent territory. <br /> <br /> IMHO, the same ought to be sayable of the likes of Iron Man, Steel, or Hardware: powersuits should be considered Inspired Super-Science, not Powered Super-Science. Essentially, they're early VARGs, and could even be considered Advanced Super-Science if not for the fact that they're close to a century ahead of their time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Tony\u2019s scientific genius is effectively a full blown superpower though. Making him a Talent in the Nova Age means he\u2019s going to get mentally outclassed by super-intelligent Novas regularly which isn\u2019t accurate to the source material being emulated at all.<br /> <br /> (Important to remember here that while Talents and Psions/Psiads are rough equals, Novas are Tier 3, and have no pretense of standing on equal footing with Tier 2 characters).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T22:13:22-08:00","id":1270768,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Tony\u2019s a nova with (1e) mega-intelligence. We see him construct new tech and materials that even teams of baseline researchers can\u2019t copy, and he does it quickly and sometimes with improvised tools.<br /> <br /> And I tend to disagree with Dataweaver\u2019s comment about powersuits necessarily being Inspired super science. They could be (Aberrant tech rules include novas \u2018designing downwards\u2019 to make their tech more accessible) but by default they\u2019re not just a century ahead of their time. Most VARGs are considerably larger than a powersuit, and the two in the AEon book that aren\u2019t (bioVARG and miniVARG) lack the full potential that nova-developed powersuits could have. That said, the human-sized VARGs are reasonable representations of what a nova inventor could make for the masses if they chose. So yes, they\u2019re about a century ahead of their time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T22:29:54-08:00","id":1270771,"title":"","content":"Whether Batman is best represented as a Talent, a Stalwart (used here as general term for Tier 2 Eximorph), or a Nova who just invested in less overt powers, really just depends on the portrayal of Batman you are going with. Because he varies WILDLY depending on the era, who is writing him, the genre of the specific story, whether it\u2019s his own title in Gotham, or a Justice League comic, etc etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 11-26-2018, 09:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T22:30:02-08:00","id":1270772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kickstarter James</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1265932-a-glimpse-of-the-aberrant-future-re-spoilers-please?p=1269801#post1269801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It could be fun to maybe showcase some &quot;Not Quite Marvel&quot; and &quot;Not Quite DC&quot; heroes during the kickstarter to show off the system! I like this idea.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sounds like a good opportunity to update the &quot;Second-Story Man&quot; sample character from Aberrant: Underworld. (For those of you who don't casually recall obscure trivia from obscure supplements, the character in question is a semi-parody of Peter Parker, if he'd told his uncle about his powers and had been encouraged to use them for personal gain.)<br /> <br /> As for Iron Man... When it comes to Tony Stark, it's important to keep in mind that between his suits and the arc reactor, he's developed stuff that seems to be able to stand up to -- or at least alongside -- Asgardian sufficiently-advanced technology. Personally, when I think of a Talent developing equipment for superheroics, I think more along the lines of the Nolan Batman Trilogy version of Lucius Fox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T22:33:58-08:00","id":1270774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1265932-a-glimpse-of-the-aberrant-future-re-spoilers-please?p=1270768#post1270768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Tony\u2019s a nova with (1e) mega-intelligence. We see him construct new tech and materials that even teams of baseline researchers can\u2019t copy, and he does it quickly and sometimes with improvised tools.<br /> <br /> And I tend to disagree with Dataweaver\u2019s comment about powersuits necessarily being Inspired super science. They could be (Aberrant tech rules include novas \u2018designing downwards\u2019 to make their tech more accessible) but by default they\u2019re not just a century ahead of their time. Most VARGs are considerably larger than a powersuit, and the two in the AEon book that aren\u2019t (bioVARG and miniVARG) lack the full potential that nova-developed powersuits could have. That said, the human-sized VARGs are reasonable representations of what a nova inventor could make for the masses if they chose. So yes, they\u2019re about a century ahead of their time.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u201c100 years more advanced\u201d I would assume doesn\u2019t translate perfectly to tech available in the Aeon era, right? It means \u201ctheoretical tech that baselines would reasonably develop over the next hundred years [i.e. in reality].\u201d Aeon era is full of tech that required Nova invention, or alien origin, to facilitate certain advances that may be less than perfectly realistic for the early 22nd century (barring AI singularity).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T06:53:07-08:00","id":1270817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1265932-a-glimpse-of-the-aberrant-future-re-spoilers-please?p=1269398#post1269398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My hopes:<br /> <br /> Aberrant 1e came out before the Marvel Cinematic Universe. These days, Iron Man isn't an obscure B-List hero known only to comic book fans; he's front and center in popular culture. So Aberrant 2e needs to make Superscience more of a thing: heroes like Iron Man and Ant-Man need to be doable without resorting to calling them Stealth Novas.<br /> <br /> Likewise, street vigilantes and superspies should get some more support, again without calling them Stealth Novas.<br /> <br /> The above can be achieved to a large extent by referencing the Talents section of the core book; so it shouldn't take much in the way of page count. Just emphasize that Talents are right there alongside the Novas making an impression on the world.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I always liked the term &quot;Elite&quot; for the so-called Stealth Novas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T22:28:51-08:00","id":1271379,"title":"","content":"Elites are already a thing in universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T22:31:26-08:00","id":1271381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>karpomatic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1265932-a-glimpse-of-the-aberrant-future-re-spoilers-please?p=1270817#post1270817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I always liked the term &quot;Elite&quot; for the so-called Stealth Novas.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Elites are Nova mercenaries, so that would be a bit confusing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T17:32:26-08:00","id":1272083,"title":"","content":"What I really hope is that what Scale is and how it should play out in-game is clearly described, with examples and handy benchmarks. It seems to me that people are still confused about how Scale operates, and how awesome Talents, Psions, and Novas are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-01T07:21:41-08:00","id":1272173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1265932-a-glimpse-of-the-aberrant-future-re-spoilers-please?p=1272083#post1272083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I really hope is that what Scale is and how it should play out in-game is clearly described, with examples and handy benchmarks. It seems to me that people are still confused about how Scale operates, and how awesome Talents, Psions, and Novas are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely second this. After seeing Scion (which is terrific for its genre) I\u2019m a little worried about not having definitive benchmarks for things like super strength or speed, or enough granularity in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3631-adamrice","name":"AdamRice","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}